      "summary": "Trough zither made of wood with parallel long sides and rounded ends. The central section is hollowed and acts as the resonator. Three equally spaced four-pointed stars are cut out of base of zither. Single length of fibre is secured at one end, stretched along trough and over cane bridges at either end; looped around deep end serrations to form seven strings. Sloping sides and back of zither decorated with alternating natural and blackened triangles. The natural triangles have horizontal grooves.",
